Subject: [PATCH] arc: 0008-server-reasoning-included (trust the server's usage
 to count past reasoning)

`features.server_reasoning_included = true` makes the context check treat the
provider's usage as already counting the earlier reasoning items it is sent
back, as if every response carried `x-reasoning-included`.

Upstream adds, for every reasoning item with `encrypted_content` before the
last user message, `(len * 3 / 4 - 650) / 4` tokens on top of the last usage
(`ContextManager::get_total_token_usage(false)`), because OpenAI's own server
does not count them. sglang does: the request after a mid-turn user message
grows by that message only. Normally the only user message is the kickoff and
the term is 0; 0005's pre-compaction reminder is a user message, so right after
it every earlier reasoning item is re-counted (median +11k tokens on the Kaggle
arm) and auto-compaction fires about one response after the reminder, at ~92k
real tokens instead of 100k. `exec resume` (a new user message) does the same
to the pre-turn check.

- `Session::get_total_token_usage` is the only reader of the per-stream flag,
  so the override there covers every writer: the reset to false at each turn
  start (`tasks/regular.rs`), the response header and the compaction stream.
- `Feature::ServerReasoningIncluded`, under development and off by default
  (the upstream behaviour is right for OpenAI's server).
